  "ingredients": [
    "2 tablespoon coconut oil",
    "2 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes",
    "2 teaspoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "1/2 medium shallot (finely diced)",
    "2 teaspoon dried oregano",
    "1/2 cup low-carb tomato sauce (like Rao's)",
    "1 tablespoon chipotle peppers in adobo sauce (chopped)",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "2 cup mexican-style cheese blend",
    "4 large egg",
    "1 medium avocado (sliced)",
    "1/2 medium lime (sliced into wedges)",
    "1/4 cup fresh cilantro (chopped)"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Over medium, heat coconut oil then add crushed red pepper flakes until shimmering. Remove from heat. Let sit for a few minutes to infuse flavor. Strain and discard solids.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat most of the chili oil over medium. Add shallots and onion. Sautee until aromatic. Add oregano, tomato sauce, and chipotle chili. Continue to cook until reduced. Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using a paper towel, spread a thin coating of the remaining chili oil onto a non-stick pan. Spread an even layer of cheese on the pan, covering the bottom. Cook over low to medium-low heat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "When the cheese starts to melt and form a cohesive layer, break eggs. Cover with lid. Cook low and slow until the whites start to settle.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the whites cooked and the edges of the cheese start to peel away from the side of the pan, increase heat to medium to medium-high. Hereon, everything will cook faster. We are looking for a crisp layer of cheese.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "The “tortilla” is done when the bottom layer is uniform and golden. Repeat this process to get more cheese and egg \"tortillas\".",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/huevos-rancheros-09.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "To serve, transfer cheese and egg tortilla to a plate. Spoon some chili salsa over and sprinkle with cilantro. Serve with avocado slices and lime wedges.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/huevos-rancheros/#wprm-recipe-53247-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
